# Recipe Box API test requests, Week 10 (Supabase edition)
#
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao),
# then click "Send Request" above any block below.
# Thunder Client works too: copy the method, URL and body.
#
# Start the server first: npm run dev
# Keep the Supabase Table Editor open in a browser tab and watch the rows change.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Read: every recipe (now from the database, ordered by id)
GET {{base}}/api/recipes

### Read: one recipe by id
GET {{base}}/api/recipes/3

### Read: an id that does not exist (expect 404)
GET {{base}}/api/recipes/99

### Read: an id that is not a number (expect 404 from checkId, NOT a 500)
GET {{base}}/api/recipes/two

### Create: a good recipe (expect 201, with a new id and created_at)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ramen",
  "cuisine": "Japanese",
  "minutes": 40,
  "tags": ["noodles"]
}

### Create: a bad recipe (expect 400 with a list of problems)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "minutes": "forty"
}

### Create: minutes is not a whole number (expect 400; the column is an integer)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Half Soup",
  "cuisine": "French",
  "minutes": 12.5
}

### Create: trying to choose our own id (expect 201, and the database ignores it)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 500,
  "name": "Sneaky Stew",
  "cuisine": "Irish",
  "minutes": 90
}

### Update: change one field (expect 200 with the updated row)
PATCH {{base}}/api/recipes/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minutes": 45
}

### Update: an id that does not exist (expect 404)
PATCH {{base}}/api/recipes/99
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minutes": 45
}

### Delete (expect 204, then run it again for a 404)
DELETE {{base}}/api/recipes/4

### Filters (Gold): vegetarian and 30 minutes or less
GET {{base}}/api/recipes?tag=vegetarian&maxMinutes=30

### Filters (Gold): cuisine, any capitalization
GET {{base}}/api/recipes?cuisine=thai

### Filters (Gold): name contains
GET {{base}}/api/recipes?q=ram

### A route that does not exist (expect JSON 404)
GET {{base}}/api/desserts

### THE RESTART TEST: stop the server (Ctrl+C), start it again (npm run dev),
### then run the first request again. Ramen is still there. Last week it was not.

### Thursday, after add-servings.sql and new types: create with servings (expect 201)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tomato Soup",
  "cuisine": "French",
  "minutes": 30,
  "servings": 4
}
